<PageLayout
  title="Potent, but not precise"
  kicker="The selectivity problem"
  description="There are potent melanocortin drugs that build pigment — afamelanotide, dersimelagon, the grey-market Melanotan II — but not one that switches on MC1R alone. Why a selective MC1R agonist, a truly clean tanning drug, is so hard to make: five receptors that all read the same four-letter key."
  thread="The body never cut a key for one door. It wrote a single word — protect, feed, calm — and trusted each tissue to listen for its own. Our drugs are still learning that economy."
